0":925,"1151":50,"1152":0,"1153":80,"1154":71,"1155":1038,"1156":104,"1157":927,"1158":39,"1159":38,"1160":1128,"1161":996,"1162":1159,"1163":997,"1164":1153,"1165":352,"1166":1129,"1167":153,"1168":343,"1169":1032,"1170":152,"1171":107,"1172":55,"1173":143,"1174":21,"1175":146,"1176":25,"1177":22,"1178":103},"orderedDocs":[[1152,"**Access** has **Sync watchlist**, which requests what they add, and **Require approval**, which holds their requests in the approval queue."],[832,"**All seasons pilot rolling** starts with the first episode of every season. Watching a season's first episode adds the rest of that season, in any order."],[758,"**Always require approval** holds matching requests in the approval queue, even from users who can request freely. **Approval reason** is shown to admins on the held request."],[852,"**API key** is in Sonarr or Radarr under Settings > General."],[1082,"**Application log level** sets how much Pulsarr records, from **Fatal** to **Trace**, or **Silent** to record nothing. Raise it to **Debug** when you're chasing a problem, and set it back afterwards. A `logLevel` set in `.env` replaces this every time Pulsarr starts."],[889,"**Apprise URLs** under **System notifications** is where admin notifications go. Enter an Apprise URL, for example `tgram://bot_token/chat_id`, and select **Add URL** for each extra one. With an email sender set, a plain email address works too. The Apprise documentation lists the URL format for every service."],[957,"**Apprise**, Apprise URLs, or email addresses when an email sender is set. These need an Apprise server."],[1023,"**Approve automatically when a quota resets** approves requests held for quota, oldest first, once the user has room again. It works whether or not expiration is on."],[1022,"**Approve automatically** approves it and sends it where it was routed."],[999,"**Approve** sends it to the Sonarr or Radarr instance shown under **Where it will go**."],[971,"**Auth header**, optional. Fill in both **Header name** and **Header value**, for example `Authorization` and `Bearer <token>`, and Pulsarr sends it with every request."],[839,"**Automatic reset** resets shows with no watching or changes for the **Inactivity period**. **Check every** sets how often Pulsarr looks for them."],[911,"**Availability notifications** decides whether users are told when something they asked for is ready. Each user still picks their own channels on their page under Plex users."],[1044,"**Bypass approval over the limit** sends requests over the limit straight through, and turns the cap off."],[870,"**Bypass ignored** adds content even when it's on the instance's import list exclusions."],[759,"**Bypass user quotas** means matching requests don't count toward the requester's quota."],[1045,"**Cap the watchlist** and **Watchlist cap** skip new watchlist items past the cap. These fields show only while **Limit requests** is on."],[828,"**Check now** reads what's playing on Plex straight away."],[781,"**Clean up approval records** removes approval records for deleted content and content already gone."],[1129,"**Clean up orphaned labels on sync** removes labels for users who were deleted, renamed or stopped syncing. **Reset labels before each sync** applies the rule above to leftover labels before each sync. Turn it on after you move away from **Keep the label**."],[1132,"**Clean up orphaned labels** deletes labels of removed, renamed or non-syncing users. **Remove all Pulsarr labels** strips every label Pulsarr added, user and tag labels alike. Other labels and your content aren't touched."],[1174,"**Clean up orphaned tags on sync** removes the tags of users who were deleted or renamed in Plex."],[1177,"**Clean up orphaned tags** deletes tags left behind by users who were removed or renamed."],[1094,"**Connection** starts on **Automatic**, which lets Pulsarr pick the best connection to your server. Choose **Address** to enter it yourself. **Test connection** checks it."],[1051,"**Count requests from the last** is the weekly rolling window, in days."],[1176,"**Create missing tags** adds a tag in each instance for any user who doesn't have one yet."],[805,"**Current watchlisters** adds one exclusion for each user who has it watchlisted. Someone who adds it later can request it again."],[407,"**Customize home** opens the cards as a board of rows. Drag a row by its handle to move it, or drag a card into another row. Full-width cards move with their row. **Hide** puts a card under **Hidden cards**, **Show** brings it back, and **Reset layout** restores the default. Changes apply as you make them. Select **Done** to close."],[1047,"**Daily** resets at midnight, server time."],[772,"**Decide by** sets what counts as no longer wanted:"],[779,"**Delete continuing shows** removes every other show."],[778,"**Delete ended shows** removes shows Sonarr marks as ended."],[1025,"**Delete expired records after** removes expired requests older than this from **History**. Cleanup only runs while **Expire approval requests** is on."],[780,"**Delete files** also deletes the media files from disk. It's on by default."],[777,"**Delete movies** removes movies from Radarr."],[1001,"**Delete** removes the record without refusing anything. The title can come back as a new request, and anything already sent to Sonarr or Radarr stays there."],[1000,"**Deny** sends nothing and moves it to **History** as denied. You can add a reason for your records before you confirm."],[956,"**Discord webhooks**, the webhook URLs of the channels to post in."],[1159,"**Edit quotas** sets or removes their quotas."],[1158,"**Edit settings** changes access and notifications for all of them. Fields left as is keep each user's current value. **Clear values** removes their alias, Discord user ID or Apprise URL."],[892,"**Email sender** takes a `mailtos://` URL for an account that can send mail, for example `mailtos://user:app_password@gmail.com`. With it set, any Apprise field in Pulsarr also accepts a plain email address, and Pulsarr sends to it through that account. Gmail needs an app password. The email sender doesn't work with saved Apprise configs."],[806,"**Everyone** adds one exclusion that blocks it for all users."],[804,"**Exclude for** decides what Pulsarr adds when Maintainerr deletes a title:"],[1019,"**Expire approval requests** closes pending requests that wait too long for a decision. **Expire after** sets how long a request can wait."],[831,"**First season rolling** starts with the whole first season, then adds later seasons the same way."],[798,"**For everyone.** Select **Exclude for everyone** from the row's menu. It also blocks anyone who adds the title later, and it stays until you select **Remove global exclusion**."],[797,"**For one user.** Expand the title's row and select **Exclude** next to the user. **Remove** undoes it. This kind clears itself when the user removes the title from their watchlist, so adding it again later works normally."],[1142,"**Friend** is a Plex friend with access to your server."],[1131,"**Full sync** rechecks every watchlisted item and fixes its labels. It needs labeling on. **Run on a schedule** runs it at the time and, if you like, the day of the week set in **Run at**, in the server's time zone."],[747,"**Genres**. When a condition checks for anime, Pulsarr also looks the title up in the community anime list and adds an \"anime\" genre if it's there."],[1151,"**Identity** shows their **Plex username**, which can't be changed here, and an **Alias** shown instead of it in Pulsarr and notifications."],[752,"**IMDb rating**, with an optional **Minimum votes**, **RT critic score**, **RT audience score** and **TMDB rating**."],[1146,"**Incoming** is a friend request they sent you. Accept it in Plex."],[1083,"**Initial lines** is how many earlier lines load when you open the page."],[1127,"**Keep the label** keeps it as a record of who asked."],[1172,"**Keep the tag** keeps it as a record of who asked."],[1125,"**Label behavior** decides what happens to a user's label when they remove the item:"],[1123,"**Label content in Plex** labels each item with who watchlists it, once the item is in Plex. A label is the **Prefix** and the user's name, for example `pulsarr:jamie`. **Name from** picks **Username** or **Alias**. Labels also apply when Sonarr or Radarr reports an import to Pulsarr."],[1041,"**Limit requests** turns the quota on."],[834,"**Manage enrollment** lists the shows Pulsarr sent to Sonarr. Select shows, pick a **Rolling mode** and apply it. Enrolled shows keep their progress unless you turn on **Start over from the beginning**, which unmonitors every episode and deletes the files beyond the mode's starting point."],[1147,"**Managed** is a Plex Home account without a watchlist."],[995,"**Manual flag**. The user has **Require approval** turned on."],[1021,"**Mark as expired** closes the request and sends nothing to Sonarr or Radarr."],[744,"**Match** decides whether a request must meet **All** of the conditions or **Any** of them. Each condition is a field, an operator and a value, for example **Year** **is above** 2000. **Add condition** adds another. **Add group** adds a nested set with its own **All** or **Any**. **Not** reverses a condition or a whole group."],[786,"**Max deletion** aborts a run that would delete more than this percentage of eligible items, meaning items of the types chosen under **What may be deleted**."],[866,"**Minimum availability** is **Announced**, **In cinemas** or **Released**."],[863,"**Monitor new items** decides whether seasons that air later are monitored."],[867,"**Monitor** is **Movie only**, **Movie and collection** or **None**."],[826,"**Monitored users**. Leave it empty to monitor everyone."],[1049,"**Monthly** resets at midnight, server time, on the day you choose."],[400,"**Most active** shows who requests the most."],[1154,"**Movies** and **Shows** set their quota and watchlist cap."],[850,"**Name** is shown across Pulsarr, for example in the Content router."],[969,"**Name**, any label you like."],[399,"**Needs your approval** lists requests waiting in the approval queue."],[906,"**New episode threshold** is how recently an episode must have aired to skip the wait and notify straight away. Older episodes, such as a back catalog being imported, are grouped."],[698,"**New user defaults.** Pulsarr adds users on its own. Each time it syncs, any Plex friend it hasn't seen before becomes a Pulsarr user with these settings. That includes everyone found by the first sync in the next step. **Sync watchlist** is on by default, so their watchlists are read. Turn on **Require approval** if you want to approve each request first, or **Limit requests** under **Movies** and **Shows** to give new users a quota."],[1144,"**No friend** has access to your server but isn't a Plex friend."],[1143,"**No server** is a Plex friend without server access. Their requests sync, but they can't watch."],[406,"**Notifications** counts what was sent, and through which channels."],[1153,"**Notifications** has their **Discord user ID** and **Apprise URL**, and switches for **Discord**, **Discord mention**, **Apprise** and **Plex mobile**. **Send a test** sends through the channels saved for them."],[1141,"**Owner** is your own Plex account."],[1062,"**Password** takes a **New password** and **Confirm new password**. Leave both blank to keep your current one."],[1145,"**Pending** is a friend request you sent that they haven't accepted."],[830,"**Pilot rolling** starts with the first episode. Watching it adds the rest of the season, and later seasons are added as viewers near the end of each one."],[725,"**Playlist protection** matches the **Playlist name** exactly, including case, in each user's own Plex account. Items in a playlist with any other spelling aren't protected."],[785,"**Playlist protection** skips anything in a Plex playlist named exactly the **Playlist name**, in any user's account. Each run creates the playlist for users who don't have it yet."],[693,"**Plex account.** Select **Open plex.tv/link** and approve the code. To paste a Plex token instead, use the **Paste a token** tab."],[749,"**Plex list**, a custom Plex list owned by the requester."],[1096,"**Plex live connection** shows whether Pulsarr is getting live updates from your server. While it's down, Pulsarr polls Plex instead."],[694,"**Plex server.** The connection starts on **Automatic**, which lets Pulsarr pick the best connection. Select **Test connection** to check it, then **Continue**. Choose **Address** only if you want to enter the server address yourself."],[827,"**Polling interval**. Pulsarr normally gets playback from the live Plex connection, and only polls at this interval while that connection is down."],[404,"**Popularity rankings** list the most watchlisted movies and shows. Select a title to see its details, where it streams, and its state in Pulsarr and in your instances."],[1061,"**Profile** has the **Email** and **Username** you sign in with."],[840,"**Progressive cleanup** deletes earlier seasons once no viewer is still on them."],[857,"**Quality profile** and **Root folder**."],[905,"**Queue wait time** is how long Pulsarr waits to collect episodes before it sends."],[996,"**Quota exceeded**. The request put the user over their quota."],[1056,"**Quota maintenance** runs that cleanup. **Run on a schedule** turns it on or off, and **Run at** sets the time, in the server's time zone."],[1042,"**Quota period** is **Daily**, **Weekly rolling** or **Monthly**."],[697,"**Radarr.** The same as Sonarr."],[401,"**Recent requests** lists the latest requests with their status. You can filter by status and change the sort order."],[825,"**Remaining episodes threshold**. A **Pilot rolling** or **First season rolling** show gets its next season when this many episodes of the current one are left."],[1178,"**Remove all user tags** strips every user tag from movies and shows. Your content isn't touched. **Also delete the tag definitions** removes the tags themselves from Sonarr and Radarr too."],[1156,"**Remove friend** ends the Plex friendship. Their Pulsarr record, watchlist and quotas are deleted at the next sync."],[1046,"**Remove quotas** deletes the user's quotas and caps. It can also approve the requests their quota was holding."],[1126,"**Remove the label** removes it."],[1171,"**Remove the tag** removes it."],[402,"**Request pipeline** counts requests at each stage. **Requested** means it's in Sonarr or Radarr with no file yet. **Grabbed** means it's downloaded but nobody has been told. **Notified** means it's ready and the user was told. Its **Placements by instance** section shows the same stages for each Sonarr and Radarr instance."],[403,"**Request to ready** shows how long movies and shows take to become available."],[1043,"**Requests per period** is the limit."],[1113,"**Require approval** holds every request from new users in the approval queue."],[1052,"**Reset on day** is the monthly reset day."],[836,"**Reset show** returns it to its mode's starting point. Episode files rolling added are deleted and viewing progress is cleared."],[783,"**Respect user sync settings** counts only the watchlists of users with sync on."],[1070,"**Revoke** cuts off anything using a key straight away, and it can't be undone."],[994,"**Router rule**. A Content router route asked for approval."],[788,"**Run now** runs once with the saved settings. **Run on a schedule** runs it at the **Day and time** you choose. Deleting can't be undone, so do a dry run first."],[858,"**Search on add** searches as soon as an item is added."],[864,"**Season folders** puts each season in its own folder."],[861,"**Season monitoring** picks which episodes to monitor. The rolling options, **Pilot rolling**, **First season rolling** and **All seasons pilot rolling**, start small and monitor more as people watch. They stay disabled until session monitoring is on."],[756,"**Season** checks every season number the show has. **is not** and **is none of** match only when no season does, the rest match when any season does. **Series status** is **Continuing**, **Ended**, **Upcoming** or **Deleted**. **Movie status** is **TBA**, **Announced**, **In cinemas**, **Released** or **Deleted**. **Streaming services** counts subscription streaming only. **Plex list** ignores case and surrounding spaces."],[929,"**Send a test direct message** messages one Discord user through the bot to check it works."],[948,"**Send a test push** pushes to one user's Plex app to check it works."],[1024,"**Send approval notifications to** picks where admins hear about requests that need a decision. The choices are **All channels**, **Apprise only**, **Discord webhook and direct messages**, **Discord direct messages only**, **Discord webhook only** and **None**. Set up the channels themselves under **Notifications**."],[1057,"**Send cap notifications to** picks where admins hear that a user reached their watchlist cap. **Notify the user** also tells the user, by Discord or Apprise if they use them."],[923,"**Send test** next to a URL posts a test message to that channel, and **Test saved URLs** tests the ones already saved."],[959,"**Send test** next to a URL sends a test announcement to it, and **Test saved URLs** tests the URLs already saved."],[890,"**Send test** next to a URL sends a test notification to it, and **Test saved URLs** tests the URLs already saved."],[973,"**Send test** posts a test event, with `\"event\": \"test\"`, to the URL and header as typed. Save the endpoint when you're done."],[789,"**Send the run summary to** picks where each run's summary goes, dry runs included. **Only when something was deleted** skips the summary when a run deletes nothing."],[741,"**Send to Sonarr** or **Send to Radarr** sends it to the **Instance** you pick. The route sets its own **Quality profile**, **Root folder**, **Search on add** and **Tags**, plus **Season monitoring** and **Series type** for Sonarr or **Monitor** for Radarr. Leave any but **Tags** on **Use instance default** to keep the instance's setting. An empty **Tags** list adds no tags."],[862,"**Series type** is **Standard**, **Anime** or **Daily**."],[1095,"**Skip content already on Plex** skips requests for titles already on Plex. **Servers to check** sets where Pulsarr looks, **Your server** or **Your server and shared servers**. Shared servers count only for the admin's own watchlist. If your server can't be checked, Pulsarr holds the request and tries again later instead of sending it."],[869,"**Skip content already on Plex**, under Plex connection, checks Plex servers, not Sonarr or Radarr. **Servers to check** there sets whether shared servers count, and they only count for the admin's own watchlist."],[874,"**Skip content no route matches**, when on, skips content that no route claims instead of sending it to the default."],[742,"**Skip** never sends it anywhere."],[761,"**Skip** routes always run first. A matching Skip route stops the request from going anywhere, whatever the other routes say."],[695,"**Sonarr.** Enter a **Name**, the **URL** and the **API key**, then select **Test connection**. Once it connects, pick a **Quality profile** and **Root folder** and select **Save and continue**."],[699,"**Start syncing.** Select **Sync watchlists** to read every watchlist once. When every row shows **Done**, select **Start workflow**. Leave **Start on launch** on so syncing starts again after a restart. The dialog closes and the sidebar shows **Sync running**."],[837,"**Stop rolling** stops tracking the show and drops its viewing progress. Nothing is deleted and the episodes stay in Sonarr."],[751,"**Streaming services**, where the title streams in your TMDB region."],[1128,"**Swap for a removed label** replaces it with the **Removed label** once nobody wants the item, so you can find it."],[1173,"**Swap for a removed tag** removes it, and adds the **Removed tag** once nobody wants the item, so you can find it. Delete sync in tag based mode deletes content with that tag."],[1130,"**Sync tags as labels** copies Sonarr and Radarr tags to Plex as labels, except user tags. Pulsarr pairs a Plex item with its Sonarr or Radarr entry by file path, so Plex and the arrs must see the media under the same paths. Each tag on an item becomes a label on it, with the same prefix. **Radarr tags on movies** and **Sonarr tags on shows** pick which ones."],[724,"**Sync tags as labels** pairs each Plex item with its Sonarr or Radarr entry by path. A movie needs the exact same file path in Plex and Radarr. A show matches on its folder path, or failing that on the folder name alone. Give the Plex and arr containers identical path mappings."],[1175,"**Sync tags** tags everything currently on a watchlist and clears tags that no longer apply."],[1112,"**Sync watchlist** is on by default. Turn it off to add new users without requesting what they watchlist."],[1098,"**Sync watchlists** reads your and your friends' watchlists from Plex again."],[873,"**Synced instances** also receive content that falls back to the default because no route matched, for example to keep a 4K copy. Each synced instance uses its own settings."],[1080,"**System** > **Logs** shows Pulsarr's log as it's written. Use **Search lines** and the **Level** filter to find what you need."],[774,"**Tag based** deletes anything carrying the **Removal tag**, which comes from User tags. Matching ignores case. **Required tag pattern** is an optional regular expression, and when set, content also needs a tag that matches it. Patterns use JavaScript syntax, are limited to 1024 characters, and a backtracking check rejects unsafe ones."],[1170,"**Tag behavior** decides what happens to a user's tag when they remove the item:"],[1167,"**Tag movies in Radarr** and **Tag shows in Sonarr** add a tag for each user who has the item on their watchlist."],[859,"**Tags** are added to items that reach the instance because no route matched. A matching route uses its own tags instead."],[405,"**Top genres** and **Library mix** break down what gets requested."],[784,"**Tracked content only** limits deletion to content requested through Pulsarr."],[1093,"**Unlink** removes the account. Watchlist syncing stops until you link again, and your requests and settings stay."],[909,"**Update notifications** tells you when a new Pulsarr release comes out. Pulsarr never updates itself."],[851,"**URL** is the instance's address, including the port."],[970,"**URL**, where Pulsarr posts."],[748,"**User**, the person who requested it."],[1139,"**Users** > **Plex users** lists you, your Plex friends, and anyone with access to your Plex server. Pulsarr adds friends on its own, with your new user defaults."],[908,"**Watchlist additions** tells you when a user adds something."],[773,"**Watchlist based** deletes anything that isn't on any user's watchlist."],[1015,"**Watchlist cap**. An item past the user's cap is skipped."],[1048,"**Weekly rolling** counts the requests from the last few days, today included. A request stops counting once it's older than the window."],[1053,"**When a month is too short** only matters for a reset day of the 29th or later. **Reset on the last day** resets on the month's last day, **Skip that month** waits for the next reset, and **Reset on the 1st** resets on the 1st of the following month."],[1020,"**When a request expires** decides what happens next:"],[750,"**Year**, **Language** and **Certification**."],[442,"`.env` holds your time zone and any other Pulsarr environment variables:"],[932,"`/approvals` lets you browse, approve and deny pending requests from Discord. It only answers the Discord user saved on your own Plex user, the account that owns the server."],[78,"`/health` needs no key and reports whether Pulsarr can reach its database."],[622,"`/opt/pulsarr/.env`"],[623,"`/opt/pulsarr/data/db/`"],[624,"`/opt/pulsarr/data/logs/`"],[80,"`/v1/progress` and `/v1/logs/stream` are server-sent event streams. They ask clients to reconnect after a few seconds and send a keep-alive comment about every half minute. The logs stream starts with a tail of recent lines. A reverse proxy in front of Pulsarr must not buffer them."],[643,"`~/.config/Pulsarr/.env`, created from a template the first time Pulsarr starts"],[644,"`~/.config/Pulsarr/db/`"],[645,"`~/.config/Pulsarr/logs/`"],[450,"`1.0.0` pins an exact version, and `1.0` follows the newest patch of that minor version."],[593,"`approvalExpiration`, from the **Approval settings** page. `expirationAction` is `expire` or `auto_approve`:"],[555,"`approvalNotify` takes `none`, `all`, `discord-only`, `apprise-only`, `webhook-only`, `dm-only`, `discord-webhook`, `discord-message` or `discord-both`."],[449,"`beta` is the newest pre-release."],[632,"`C:\\ProgramData\\Pulsarr\\.env`"],[633,"`C:\\ProgramData\\Pulsarr\\db\\`"],[634,"`C:\\ProgramData\\Pulsarr\\logs\\`"],[357,"`data` depends on the event. Each page here documents one event with its schema and an example. Pulsarr validates every payload against that schema before sending it, so the shape you see here is what arrives."],[651,"`dataDir` is the exception, because it decides which folder Pulsarr reads `.env` from. Set it as a real environment variable."],[443,"`docker-compose.yml`:"],[448,"`latest` is the newest release."],[451,"`node`, `beta-node`, `1.0.0-node` and `1.0-node` are the same tags for the Node.js image. It exists for hosts where the default image once failed to start, such as some Synology NAS models. That is fixed, so use the default image. The `node` tags will point at it in a future release."],[594,"`plexLabelSync`, from the **Plex labels** page:"],[595,"`plexSessionMonitoring`, from the **Session monitoring** page:"],[628,"`pulsarr-service.exe stop`, `start` and `restart` in `C:\\Program Files\\Pulsarr` do the same."],[592,"`quotaSettings`, from the **Quotas** page:"],[1077,"<Card title=\"Account\" href=\"/system/account\" description=\"Your admin email, username and password.\" />"],[1075,"<Card title=\"API keys\" href=\"/system/api-keys\" description=\"Let other apps and scripts call the Pulsarr API.\" />"],[937,"<Card title=\"Apprise\" href=\"/notifications/apprise\" description=\"Telegram, Slack, email and many other services.\" />"],[1030,"<Card title=\"Approval queue\" href=\"/requests/approval-queue\" description=\"Approve, deny or reroute requests that are waiting.\" />"],[1031,"<Card title=\"Approval settings\" href=\"/requests/approval-settings\" description=\"Expiration, approval notifications and cleanup.\" />"],[813,"<Card title=\"Content router\" href=\"/library/content-router\" description=\"Send requests to different instances based on what they are and who asked.\" />"],[815,"<Card title=\"Delete sync\" href=\"/library/delete-sync\" description=\"Remove content from Sonarr and Radarr once nobody wants it.\" />"],[941,"<Card title=\"Delivery\" href=\"/notifications/delivery\" description=\"Episode grouping, admin notices and user alerts.\" />"],[936,"<Card title=\"Discord\" href=\"/notifications/discord\" description=\"Admin webhooks, and a bot that messages users.\" />"],[600,"<Card title=\"Docker\" href=\"/installation/docker\" description=\"Compose, docker run, image tags, file ownership and updates.\" />"],[603,"<Card title=\"Environment variables\" href=\"/installation/environment-variables\" description=\"Every setting Pulsarr reads from .env, with its default.\" />"],[814,"<Card title=\"Exclusions\" href=\"/library/exclusions\" description=\"Block watchlisted titles from being requested, including after Maintainerr deletes them.\" />"],[425,"<Card title=\"How Pulsarr works\" href=\"/how-it-works\" description=\"What happens between a watchlist add and the notification that it's ready.\" />"],[427,"<Card title=\"Installation\" href=\"/installation\" description=\"Docker and the native installers for Linux, macOS and Windows, plus the Unraid and TrueNAS app catal…\" />"],[1076,"<Card title=\"Logs\" href=\"/system/logs\" description=\"Read the log as it's written, and set how much it records.\" />"],[601,"<Card title=\"Native installers\" href=\"/installation/native\" description=\"Linux, Windows and macOS builds that need no Docker.\" />"],[1105,"<Card title=\"New user defaults\" href=\"/users/new-user-defaults\" description=\"What users start with when Pulsarr first sees them.\" />"],[1074,"<Card title=\"Plex connection\" href=\"/system/plex-connection\" description=\"The Plex account and server, watchlist feeds and library refresh.\" />"],[1107,"<Card title=\"Plex labels\" href=\"/users/plex-labels\" description=\"Label movies and shows in Plex by who has them on their watchlist.\" />"],[939,"<Card title=\"Plex mobile\" href=\"/notifications/plex-mobile\" description=\"Push notifications in the Plex app.\" />"],[1104,"<Card title=\"Plex users\" href=\"/users/plex-users\" description=\"Sync, approval, notifications and quotas for each person.\" />"],[602,"<Card title=\"PostgreSQL\" href=\"/installation/postgresql\" description=\"Use PostgreSQL instead of SQLite, or move an existing install.\" />"],[940,"<Card title=\"Public content\" href=\"/notifications/public-content\" description=\"Announce every ready title in shared channels.\" />"],[426,"<Card title=\"Quick start\" href=\"/installation/quick-start\" description=\"From installing Pulsarr to your first watchlist item reaching Sonarr or Radarr.\" />"],[599,"<Card title=\"Quick start\" href=\"/installation/quick-start\" description=\"Install with Docker and run first-run setup.\" />"],[1032,"<Card title=\"Quotas\" href=\"/requests/quotas\" description=\"Request limits and watchlist caps per user.\" />"],[816,"<Card title=\"Session monitoring\" href=\"/library/session-monitoring\" description=\"Grow rolling shows in Sonarr as people watch them.\" />"],[812,"<Card title=\"Sonarr and Radarr\" href=\"/library/sonarr-radarr\" description=\"Connect instances and set where 