d:"],[1168,"A tag is the **Prefix** and the user's name, for example `pulsarr-user-jamie`. **Name from** picks **Username** or **Alias**. Users without an alias fall back to their Plex username."],[891,"A user's own Apprise URL goes on their page under Plex users, or they can set it with `/notifications` in Discord."],[475,"A variable in `.env` replaces the value saved in the app every time Pulsarr starts. This happens even when the variable is set to an empty value. A change you make in the app lasts only until the next restart, so remove the variable from `.env` if you want to manage that setting in the app."],[710,"A webhook doesn't fire or its test fails"],[1069,"A wrong or revoked key gets a 401, even on a network where sign-in is skipped."],[416,"About every two hours, Pulsarr reads every watchlist in full. That is when it notices removed titles. Everything tied to a watchlist follows the removal, such as user tags, Plex labels and what delete sync may remove."],[302,"Accepts GUID format IDs (tmdb:123, tvdb:456) and resolves to fetch TMDB metadata"],[1058,"Account"],[991,"Act on several requests"],[1165,"Actions"],[688,"Add a `docker-compose.yml` next to it:"],[702,"Add a movie to your Plex watchlist, then open Radarr. The movie shows up there once Pulsarr picks up the change. With Plex Pass that takes seconds. Without it, Pulsarr checks watchlists on a schedule."],[732,"Add a route"],[963,"Add an endpoint"],[844,"Add an instance"],[660,"Add the connection to `.env` before Pulsarr starts for the first time:"],[665,"Add the PostgreSQL settings above to `.env`."],[901,"Admin notifications"],[914,"Admin webhooks"],[692,"After you sign in, the setup dialog opens. It has six steps. The other steps stay locked until you link a Plex account."],[687,"Almost every Pulsarr setting can also be set in `.env`, as listed in environment variables. For this guide, the time zone is all you need."],[650,"Almost every setting can also be set in `.env`. See environment variables 