ad, Pulsarr skips the ownership change. `./data` must then already be writable by that user, or the container stops with an error."],[808,"If you use Maintainerr this way, consider turning delete sync off and keeping your removal rules in Maintainerr, so only one tool removes content."],[435,"Image tags"],[921,"In Discord, open the channel's settings, then **Integrations** > **Webhooks** > **New Webhook**, and copy its URL."],[803,"In the **Maintainerr** section, turn on **Use Maintainerr**, enter the **Maintainerr URL** and save. Pulsarr then sets up a webhook named \"Pulsarr\" in Maintainerr and connects it to the rule groups whose collections delete media. Groups that only unmonitor aren't connected, because the webhook doesn't say which action ran. Pulsarr reconnects on its own on a schedule, and **Sync now** does it straight away."],[924,"In the Discord Developer Portal, create a new application. You can use the Pulsarr icon as its picture."],[675,"Install Pulsarr"],[607,"Install Pulsarr on Linux, Windows or macOS without Docker."],[673,"Install Pulsarr with Docker and get your first watchlist item into Sonarr or Radarr."],[597,"Install Pulsarr with Docker or the native installers, or find it in the Unraid and TrueNAS app catalogs."],[596,"Installation"],[419,"Introduction"],[668,"It checks both connections, backs up the SQLite database to `./data/backups/`, copies every table and checks that the row counts match. After the copy it moves each PostgreSQL ID sequence up to the highest copied ID, so new rows don't collide. It refuses a table that already has rows and stops at the first table that fails. After a failed run, recreate the database and run step 4 again."],[617,"It installs the latest release to `/opt/pulsarr`, creates a `pulsarr` system user, and starts Pulsarr as a systemd service. On systems without systemd, use Docker instead."],[473,"JSON settings"],[1116,"Label movies and shows in Plex by who has them on their watchlist."],[1117,"Labeling"],[723,"Labels and user tags apply only to items on a user's watchlist. Labels need the Plex connection and appear once the item is in Plex. User tags apply when watchlists sync, or straight away with **Sync tags**."],[711,"Labels or tags don't appear"],[1066,"Let other apps and scripts call the Pulsarr API."],[809,"Library"],[30,"Lightweight endpoint to verify the current session is authenticated"],[1034,"Limit how many movies and shows each user can request, and cap the size of their watchlist."],[74,"Limits and paging"],[1086,"Link the Plex account and server Pulsarr reads watchlists through, and set up library refresh."],[608,"Linux"],[385,"List all available webhook event types with descriptions"],[120,"List and probe every connection to the Plex servers a token owns"],[341,"List watchlist items with their exclusion state"],[382,"List webhook endpoints"],[384,"List webhook event types"],[75,"Live streams"],[1078,"Logs"],[610,"macOS"],[635,"macOS 13 (Ventura) or later is required."],[471,"Maintainerr"],[794,"Maintainerr"],[807,"Maintainerr only adds exclusions. Remove them on this page."],[821,"Manage enrollment"],[647,"Manage it with `launchctl stop com.pulsarr` and `launchctl start com.pulsarr`. `KeepAlive` restarts Pulsarr whenever it stops, so to keep it stopped run `launchctl unload ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.pulsarr.plist` instead of `pkill`."],[627,"Manage the service in `services.msc`, or from an administrator prompt:"],[618,"Manage the service with `systemctl`:"],[240,"Manually trigger the Plex session monitoring process to check for viewing activity and update rolling monitored shows"],[366,"Media available"],[945,"Mobile app setup"],[766,"Mode"],[819,"Monitoring"],[655,"Move from SQLite"],[958,"Movies and shows use their own tab's lists when they have any, and the **All content** lists otherwise. They never get both."],[606,"Native installers"],[598,"New to Pulsarr? Start with the quick start. It goes from install to your first watchlist item reaching Sonarr or Radarr."],[472,"New user defaults"],[1108,"New user defaults"],[1136,"Not yet friends"],[1003,"Notes you add stay with the request and appear in webhook notifications. The requester never sees them."],[776,"Nothing outside these choices is deleted:"],[468,"Notifications"],[770,"Notifications"],[933,"Notifications"],[1010,"Notifications"],[926,"On **OAuth2** > **URL Generator**, select the `bot` and `applications.commands` scopes. The bot needs no permissions, because it only answers its own slash commands and sends direct messages."],[960,"On Discord, the announcement mentions the users who have the title on their watchlist, if they have **Discord mention** turned on and a **Discord user ID** saved on their page under Plex users."],[659,"On PostgreSQL 15 and later, `GRANT ALL PRIVILEGES ON DATABASE` does not allow creating tables in the `public` schema, so make the user the owner instead."],[728,"On PostgreSQL 15 and later, create the database with `OWNER` instead of granting privileges on it. Create the tables before copying the data. The copy refuses tables that already have rows, so after a failed run recreate the database and start from the table step. See PostgreSQL."],[925,"On the **Bot** page, turn on **Message Content Intent** and copy the bot token."],[872,"Only the default instance has these two settings:"],[429,"Only use the issue tracker if you've found a bug or have a specific feature request."],[691,"Open `http://<your-server>:3003`. On first visit Pulsarr asks you to create the admin account. Fill in **Email**, **Username**, **Password** and **Confirm password**, then select **Create account**. Sign in with the new account."],[1040,"Open a user from **Users** > **Plex users**. Movies and shows have separate quotas. To set quotas for several users at once, select them on **Plex users** and use **Edit quotas**. New users get the quotas set on New user defaults."],[639,"Open Pulsarr. It runs in the background, with no window or Dock icon."],[637,"Open the DMG and drag **Pulsarr** to **Applications**."],[927,"Open the generated URL and add the bot to your server."],[661,"Or give the whole connection as `dbConnectionString=postgresql://user:password@host:5432/pulsarr`, which is used instead of the separate settings. Pulsarr sets up the tables when it starts."],[736,"Order and priority"],[1008,"Order of checks"],[342,"Page through watchlisted and excluded titles, one row per title with its watchlisters and own exclusions attached"],[140,"Parse and process RSS feed watchlist items"],[139,"Parse RSS watchlists"],[922,"Paste it into **Webhook URLs** in Pulsarr. To post to several channels, select **Add URL** and paste each one into its own field."],[965,"Payloads"],[208,"Perform a dry-run of the delete sync job to preview what would be deleted. Holds the request open for the whole run, so use POST /v1/scheduler/schedules/delete-sync/dry-run/start instead."],[156,"Perform bulk quota operations on multiple users (update or delete)"],[18,"Permanently delete an approval request from database"],[465,"Plex"],[1087,"Plex account"],[951,"Plex can also notify about every new item in a library, under **New Content Added to Library**. With that on, users get two notifications for the same title. Unchecking all libraries there leaves only Pulsarr's, which only cover what's on their watchlist."],[1085,"Plex connection"],[1115,"Plex labels"],[1122,"Plex labels mark each movie and show in Plex with the users who have it on their watchlist. Set them up under **Users** > **Plex labels**."],[1090,"Plex library refresh"],[707,"Plex live connection shows Polling"],[942,"Plex mobile"],[708,"Plex mobile notifications are missing or doubled"],[720,"Plex mobile notifications need Plex Pass on the server, and users need notifications turned on in the Plex app. Doubles come from the Plex app's own new content notifications, which users turn off per library in the app. See Plex mobile."],[1088,"Plex server"],[1133,"Plex users"],[143,"Poll Plex PIN for auth token"],[613,"Portable zips"],[438,"Ports"],[962,"Post a JSON payload to your own service when something happens in Pulsarr."],[108,"Post a test message to a Discord webhook URL, saved or not"],[913,"Post admin notifications to Discord channels, and message users through a bot."],[897,"Posters and other images only come through with Apprise API 1.5.0 or later."],[652,"PostgreSQL"],[197,"Probe Radarr routing options"],[255,"Probe Sonarr routing options"],[93,"Process Maintainerr webhook"],[95,"Process media webhook"],[94,"Process MEDIA_HANDLED webhooks from Maintainerr (3.23.0+) to exclude handled media from watchlist syncing. Requires the webhook secret in the Authorization header."],[96,"Process webhooks from Radarr (movies) or Sonarr (TV series) for media notifications. Requires X-Pulsarr-Secret header for authentication."],[102,"Provision the Maintainerr webhook configuration and rule group connections now"],[952,"Public content"],[954,"Public content announces every title that becomes available, whoever asked for it, in shared channels. Users still get their own notifications. Set it up under **Notifications** > **Public content** and turn on **Broadcast to shared channels**."],[457,"Pull the new image and recreate the container:"],[1103,"Pulsarr adds your Plex friends as users on its own. These pages set what each user can do and mark their requests in Sonarr, Radarr and Plex."],[71,"Pulsarr API"],[802,"Pulsarr can add exclusions for media that Maintainerr deletes, so stale watchlists don't request it again. It needs Maintainerr 3.23.0 or later, and Maintainerr must be able to reach Pulsarr."],[423,"Pulsarr can only read the watchlist of someone who is a friend of your Plex account. People with access to your server who aren't friends yet show up under **Not yet friends** on the **Plex users** page, where you can send them a friend request."],[1148,"Pulsarr can only read the watchlists of your Plex friends. People it can't track yet show under **Not yet friends**, except **Managed** accounts. Select **Send friend request** for a **No friend** account, or **Cancel request** or **Resend request** for a **Pending** one."],[1014,"Pulsarr checks each new watchlist item in this order."],[986,"Pulsarr checks HTTPS certificates, so an endpoint with a self-signed certificate fails."],[721,"Pulsarr checks the Apprise server only while it starts. Start Apprise first, or restart Pulsarr once Apprise is up. In the same Compose file, `appriseUrl` uses the container name and port, for example `http://apprise:8000`."],[658,"Pulsarr creates the tables, but not the database. Create an empty database owned by your user first:"],[505,"Pulsarr generates the secrets on first start and stores them, so they stay the same across restarts. Set them in `.env` only if you need fixed values."],[631,"Pulsarr installs to `C:\\Program Files\\Pulsarr`. Where files live:"],[604,"Pulsarr is also in the Unraid Community Applications and TrueNAS community app catalogs. Search for Pulsarr in either one."],[689,"Pulsarr keeps its database and logs in `./data`."],[355,"Pulsarr posts these payloads to the endpoints you add under Webhooks. They are outgoing requests from Pulsarr to your service, so no API key is involved. If you set an auth header on the endpoint, Pulsarr sends it with every request."],[946,"Pulsarr pushes a notification to a user's Plex mobile app when something on their watchlist becomes available. Tapping it opens the title in Plex. It needs Plex Pass on your server."],[446,"Pulsarr reads its settings from the container's environment. `env_file` passes `.env` into it, so the file must sit next to `docker-compose.yml`. A `.env` inside `./data` is not read. A variable can also go under `environment:`, which wins when both set it."],[474,"Pulsarr reads these from `.env`, or from the container's environment in Docker. Most of them are also settings in the app, and you only need `.env` to fix a value before first start or to keep it under version control."],[1092,"Pulsarr reads watchlists through the Plex account that owns your server. To link a different account, select **Relink with Plex** and approve Pulsarr on plex.tv, or **Paste a token** if you already have one."],[684,"Pulsarr reads your own watchlist and the watchlists of your Plex friends. Anyone who isn't a friend of your Plex account is skipped."],[415,"Pulsarr reads your watchlist from Plex's watchlist API and your friends' watchlists from Plex's community GraphQL API. The RSS feeds only speed up noticing changes. With Plex Pass, Pulsarr watches the watchlist RSS feeds about every ten seconds and fetches new items from those APIs. The feeds are static files that Plex regenerates when a watchlist changes and serves from a content delivery network, built to keep polling off Plex's own servers, so checking them this often is safe. Without Plex Pass, it polls the same APIs for changes about every five minutes."],[453,"Pulsarr runs as the user and group set by `PUID` and `PGID`, which both default to `1000`. On start it takes ownership of anything in `./data` that has a different owner. Set them to your user on the host, which `id -u` and `id -g` print."],[1029,"Pulsarr sends most watchlist items straight to Sonarr or Radarr. An item waits in the approval queue instead when the user requires approval, when it puts them over their quota, or when a Content router route asks for approval."],[413,"Pulsarr sits between Plex watchlists and Sonarr and Radarr. Users add titles to their watchlist in Plex. Pulsarr requests them and tells users when they're ready."],[935,"Pulsarr tells users when something they asked for is ready, and tells admins about requests, deletions and updates."],[510,"Pulsarr trusts forwarded headers only from loopback, link-local and private addresses. The proxy must send `X-Forwarded-For`, or every visitor shares the proxy's address and trips the per-IP rate limits together. Traefik, Caddy and Nginx Proxy Manager handle both headers by default. Plain nginx needs `proxy_set_header Host $host;` and `proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;`."],[418,"Pulsarr turns Plex watchlists into Sonarr and Radarr requests."],[458,"Pulsarr updates its database on start, so there's nothing else to run."],[893,"Pulsarr uses Apprise's stateless notify endpoint, so every URL you enter in Pulsarr is sent along with each notification, and nothing has to be saved in Apprise."],[657,"Pulsarr uses SQLite by default and needs no setup for it. You can use PostgreSQL instead, either from the first start or by moving an existing SQLite install across."],[522,"Pulsarr uses these only to create a first Sonarr or Radarr instance when there is none. After that, manage instances on the **Sonarr** and **Radarr** pages, and remove these variables from `.env`."],[422,"Pulsarr watches your Plex watchlist and the watchlists of your Plex friends. When a movie or show is added, Pulsarr sends it to Radarr or Sonarr. When it's available, Pulsarr can notify the person who added it through Discord, Apprise or Plex mobile push."],[943,"Push a notification to users' Plex app when something on their watchlist is ready."],[672,"Quick start"],[1017,"Quota. An item over the user's quota waits for approval, unless the user has **Bypass approval over the limit** or the route has **Bypass user quotas**."],[1033,"Quotas"],[1079,"Read Pulsarr's log as it's written, and set how much it records."],[198,"Read quality profiles, root folders and tags from a Radarr instance with unsaved credentials"],[256,"Read quality profiles, root folders and tags from a Sonarr instance with unsaved credentials"],[177,"Record quota usage"],[178,"Record quota usage for a user"],[26,"Reject an approval request (marks as rejected)"],[25,"Reject approval request"],[14,"Reject multiple approval requests in batch"],[1135,"Relationship"],[228,"Remove a show from rolling monitoring and stop tracking its viewing activity"],[344,"Remove a watchlist exclusion by ID"],[84,"Remove all Pulsarr-created labels from Plex content while preserving other labels"],[297,"Remove all user tags"],[298,"Remove all user tags from media and optionally delete tag definitions"],[847,"Remove an instance"],[1121,"Remove labels"],[765,"Remove movies and shows from Sonarr and Radarr once nobody wants them."],[145,"Remove Plex notifications"],[146,"Remove Plex webhook notifications from Radarr and Sonarr instances"],[83,"Remove Pulsarr labels from Plex content"],[334,"Remove several watchlist exclusions by ID"],[343,"Remove watchlist exclusion"],[116,"Removes a friend or cancels a pending sent friend request via the Plex removeFriend mutation"],[877,"Removing an instance also deletes the Content router routes that send to it, its place in other instances' synced instances, and Pulsarr's record of which watchlist items are on it. The watchlist items themselves stay. For Sonarr, rolling monitored shows on the instance are removed too."],[65,"Reorder router rules"],[70,"Replace an existing content router rule by its ID. The full rule payload is required - fields left out are cleared, not preserved."],[296,"Report whether user tags exist and how many items carry them per instance"],[1027,"Requests"],[79,"Requests are rate limited per IP address, with the global limit set by `rateLimitMax`. Sign-in, account changes and inbound webhooks with a bad secret have tighter limits, and webhooks with a valid secret are never limited. A `429` carries `Retry-After` and the `X-RateLimit` headers. List routes page with `limit` and `offset`."],[238,"Reset a rolling monitored show back to its original monitoring state (pilot only or first season only)"],[236,"Reset all rolling monitored shows that have been inactive for a specified number of days"],[235,"Reset inactive rolling monitored shows"],[237,"Reset rolling monitored show"],[822,"Resets and cleanup"],[476,"Restart Pulsarr after changing `.env`. Values marked JSON take one line of JSON, for exam