],[722,"The endpoint must answer with a 2xx status. Deliveries are retried only after a timeout, a network error, a 5xx or a 429, and a test is sent once with no retry. HTTPS endpoints need a trusted certificate, so a self-signed one fails."],[972,"The events to send. Pick at least one."],[700,"The first Sonarr and the first Radarr you add become the default instances. Requests go to them until you add rules in the **Content router**."],[1124,"The format can't change while Pulsarr's labels exist. Remove them first with **Remove all Pulsarr labels**."],[1169,"The format can't change while the tags exist in Sonarr or Radarr. Remove them first with **Remove all user tags** and **Also delete the tag definitions**."],[455,"The image checks `/health` on its own, so `docker ps` shows the container as healthy or unhealthy. The route needs no sign-in and returns `200` when the database answers and `503` when it does not, so a proxy status page or an uptime monitor can use it too."],[616,"The install script needs `curl`, `unzip` and systemd, and supports x64 and arm64:"],[354,"The JSON Pulsarr posts to your webhook endpoints, one page per event."],[408,"The layout is saved in your browser, so each browser keeps its own."],[1084,"The log files themselves are in the `logs` folder of Pulsarr's data folder, for example `./data/logs` in Docker."],[1155,"The page also shows what's on their watchlist, their requests by status and their quota usage."],[682,"The Plex account that owns your Plex server."],[1100,"The Plex connection Pulsarr adds uses the host, port and SSL setting of your **Address**, or of the connection **Automatic** picked. An address without a port gets 443 with SSL and 80 without."],[1072,"The Plex connection, API keys, logs and your admin account."],[716,"The PostgreSQL migration fails"],[727,"The proxy isn't sending `X-Forwarded-For`, so every visitor shares the proxy's address. See Reverse proxy."],[509,"The proxy must pass the path through unchanged, `basePath`