 address with no port is called on 443, not on Pulsarr's port. Pulsarr adds a secret header to the webhook it creates and rejects calls without it, so there is nothing to set up by hand."],[445,"Then open `http://<your-server>:3003`. Pulsarr keeps its database and logs in `./data`. To back up Pulsarr, stop the container and copy that folder."],[887,"Then point Pulsarr at it in `.env` and restart Pulsarr:"],[796,"There are two kinds:"],[838,"These decide what happens to shows nobody is watching:"],[430,"These docs are maintained on GitHub. To suggest an improvement, open an issue or pull request."],[811,"These pages control what happens after a request leaves Pulsarr. They decide which instance gets it, which titles are never requested, and when content is removed."],[1073,"These pages cover Pulsarr's link to Plex, access to its API, its log and your admin login."],[907,"These pick where notices for admins go. The choices are **All channels**, **Apprise only**, **Discord webhook and direct messages**, **Discord direct messages only**, **Discord webhook only** and **None**."],[903,"These settings apply to every notification channel. Find them under **Notifications** > **Delivery**."],[855,"These settings apply to everything Pulsarr sends to the instance. A Content router route can override **Quality profile**, **Root folder**, **Search on add** and **Tags**, plus **Season monitoring** and **Series type** for Sonarr and **Monitor** for Radarr."],[662,"These steps use Docker and the `docker-compose.migration.yml` from the repository. Put it next to your `docker-compose.yml`."],[591,"These take one line of JSON. `quotaSettings` and `plexLabelSync` fill in any field you leave out from the defaults shown. `approvalExpiration`, `plexSessionMonitoring` and `publicContentNotifications` need every field."],[679,"This guide installs Pulsarr with Docker Compose and walks through first-run setup. At the end, a title you add to your Plex watchlist shows up in Sonarr or Radarr."],[