l, so every endpoint gets its events for all users. Set them up under **Notifications** > **Webhooks**."],[417,"Welcome to Pulsarr"],[410,"What happens between someone adding a title to their Plex watchlist and being told it's ready."],[767,"What may be deleted"],[768,"What protects content"],[737,"When nothing matches"],[904,"When several episodes of a show arrive close together, Pulsarr sends one notification instead of one per episode."],[841,"When some shows are inactive, the **Rolling shows** card has a button that resets all of them at once, for example **Reset 3 inactive**."],[1118,"When something leaves a watchlist"],[1164,"When something leaves a watchlist"],[875,"When you add a synced instance, **Copy existing content** sends everything already on the default to it. New content syncs on its own."],[845,"Where content lands"],[621,"Where files live:"],[642,"Where files live:"],[810,"Where requests go in Sonarr and Radarr, what's kept out, and what's removed."],[1162,"Where to tag"],[212,"Whether a delete sync dry run is running and how the latest one ended. Resets when the server restarts."],[138,"Whether a sync of one watchlist type is running and how the latest one ended. Resets when the server restarts."],[989,"Why a request waits"],[609,"Windows"],[719,"With **Automatic**, Pulsarr uses the connections plex.tv lists for your server, and none of them may be reachable from where Pulsarr runs. Under **System** > **Plex connection**, choose **Address**, enter one Pulsarr can reach, and select **Test connection**."],[511,"With `allowedHosts` set, list the hostname the proxy serves and any name Sonarr, Radarr or Maintainerr use to reach Pulsarr directly, such as its container name. If the proxy rewrites `Host` to its upstream name, list that name too. Keeping the original with `proxy_set_header Host $host;` avoids this."],[512,"With `requiredExceptLocal`, a proxy on a private address that doesn't send `X-Forwarded-For` makes every request look local, so nobody is asked to sign in."],[507,"With `requiredExceptLocal`, also set `allowedHosts`. A site can point its own domain at your Pulsarr address, and its pages would then count as local visitors."],[1097,"With Plex Pass, Pulsarr watches two RSS feeds, **Your watchlist feed** and **Friends' watchlist feed**, so new watchlist items arrive within seconds. Without Plex Pass, Pulsarr checks each watchlist about every five minutes. **Generate feeds** asks Plex for the feed URLs. **Generate again** asks for new ones and replaces the old ones."],[424,"With Plex Pass, watchlist changes arrive within seconds. Without it, Pulsarr checks each watchlist on a schedule."],[738,"Without routes, every request goes to the default Sonarr or Radarr instance. Routes send matching requests somewhere else, with their own settings, or skip them. Manage them under **Library** > **Content router**, which has a **Movies** tab for Radarr routes and a **TV shows** tab for Sonarr routes."],[1005,"You can also approve and deny requests from Discord with the bot's `/approvals` command."],[931,"You can also paste a user's **Discord user ID** on their page under Plex users. Users get direct messages only once a Discord user ID is saved for them, and only while they share a server with the bot. A user who turns off direct messages from server members in their Discord privacy settings gets none."],[680,"You need:"],[1060,"Your admin account is the login for Pulsarr itself, separate from your Plex account. Open **Account settings** from the account menu at the bottom of the sidebar."],[985,"Your endpoint must answer with a 2xx status within about ten seconds. Timeouts, network errors, 5xx and 429 are retried for up to three attempts, a 4xx gets one attempt, and retries stop when `Retry-After` asks for more than a minute."],[930,"Your own account cannot be linked from Discord. Paste your **Discord user ID** on your page under Plex users. Everyone else runs `/notifications` in your Discord server and enters their Plex username to link their account. After that, `/notifications` lets them change their own notification settings."],[1102,"Your Plex friends, what each one can request, and how their requests are tagged and labeled."]],"type":"string"},"page_id":{"docs":{"1":24,"2":25,"3":26,"4":27,"5":28,"6":29,"7":30,"8":31,"9":32,"10":33,"11":34,"12":35,"13":36,"14":37,"15":38,"16":39,"17":40,"18":41,"19":42,"20":43,"21":44,"22":45,"23":46,"24":47,"25":48,"26":49,"27":50,"28":51,"29":52,"30":53,"31":54,"32":55,"33":56,"34":57,"35":58,"36":59,"37":60,"38":61,"39":62,"40":63,"41":64,"42":65,"43":66,"44":67,"45":68,"46":69,"47":70,"48":71,"49":72,"50":73,"51":74,"52":75,"53":76,"54":77,"55":78,"56":79,"57":80,"58":81,"59":82,"60":83,"61":84,"62":85,"63":86,"64":87,"65":88,"66":89,"67":90,"68":91,"69":92,"70":93,"71":14,"72":15,"73":16,"74":17,"75":18,"76":19,"77":20,"78":21,"79":22,"80":23,"81":94,"82":95,"83":96,"84":97,"85":98,"86":99,"87":100,"88":101,"89":102,"90":103,"91":104,"92":105,"93":106,"94":107,"95":108,"96":109,"97":110,"98":111,"99":112,"100":113,"101":114,"102":115,"103":116,"104":117,"105":118,"106":119,"107":120,"108":121,"109":122,"110":123,"111":124,"112":125,"113":126,"114":127,"115":128,"116":129,"117":130,"118":131,"119":132,"120":133,"121":134,"122":135,"123":136,"124":137,"125":138,"126":139,"127":140,"128":141,"129":142,"130":143,"131":144,"132":145,"133":146,"134":147,"135":148,"136":149,"137":150,"138":151,"139":152,"140":153,"141":154,"142":155,"143":156,"144":157,"145":158,"146":159,"147":160,"148":161,"149":162,"150":163,"151":164,"152":165,"153":166,"154":167,"155":168,"156":169,"157":170,"158":171,"159":172,"160":173,"161":174,"162":175,"163":176,"164":177,"165":178,"166":179,"167":180,"168":181,"169":182,"170":183,"171":186,"172":187,"173":184,"174":185,"175":188,"176":189,"177":190,"178":191,"179":192,"180":193,"181":194,"182":195,"183":196,"184":197,"185":198,"186":199,"187":200,"188":201,"189":202,"190":203,"191":204,"192":205,"193":206,"19